{
 "artifact_type": "omp_ninfer_measurement",
 "schema_version": 1,
 "experiment": "EXP-072",
 "title": "Stock OMP 18.4.0 long sessions on both lanes: async compaction fails a turn on the single-admission RTX 4090 lane; inline compaction survives three compactions and a restart",
 "generated_utc": "2026-09-28T14:10:00Z",
 "status": "observed",
 "question": "Does an unmodified OMP 18.4.0 session, configured only by each documented route's provider fragment and config, keep working through repeated automatic compaction and a server restart after it on both published lanes? What does each compaction cost, what does it keep, and how does it meet the runtime's durable checkpoints?",
 "answer": "Not on the RTX 4090 before this change. OMP's async compaction (on by default) starts the handoff summary in the background as a session nears its threshold. Both lanes admit one request at a time, so the user's next turn waited behind it; each attempt expired at the runtime's 30 s admission deadline and OMP resent it. The handoff resends the whole session with tool_choice none, which the runtime renders without the tool block, so it reused no cache and took 56-61 s; in the third of three epochs it outlasted OMP's resends and the turn failed with 503 request_queue_timeout. With compaction.asyncEnabled false, OMP compacts before the turn instead: three consecutive RTX 4090 handoffs committed in 77.0-83.7 s with no expired admission, the session recalled each compaction's newest identifier after it and after a graceful restart, and it still named all three older identifiers after three compactions. The RTX 5090 compacts with snapcompact on the client (0.07-0.08 s) and needs no change; its frames reach the model at native resolution and it read back both identifiers that existed only inside frames. Snapcompact keeps a bounded archive and drops the rest of the older middle by design (76,832 and 192,080 characters in the two runs).",
 "method": {
  "tool": "scripts/omp_long_session_proof.py (this release): OMP in RPC mode with PI_OPENAI_STATEFUL=1 and an isolated HOME holding the route's documented models.yml and config.yml verbatim (baseUrl substituted with the forward in use); thinking low; seeded synthetic build-log filler of 40,000 bytes per turn (about 23,600 runtime tokens). Each epoch plants a durable identifier after one filler turn and a control identifier in the turn predicted to precede OMP's threshold (131,072 less max(15%, 16,384) = 111,412 tokens); after OMP commits a compaction the session is asked for the control identifier. Gated: every turn completes, the expected method commits every compaction, the control identifier is recalled after each compaction and after the restart, one OMP session id. Recorded, not gated: all durable identifiers asked for once at the end.",
  "client": {
   "binary": "omp-darwin-arm64 from https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/releases/tag/v18.4.0 (commit 401778d0cd30020ce0f9198f751b13c68850562f)",
   "sha256": "90111c710fb861b03e5ef6fd3257319001acdd77ff7d06d3a6207996f2777709",
   "version": "omp/18.4.0"
  },
  "lanes": {
   "rtx4090": "The installed lane (release qwen38-4090-native-v0.6.9-beta.1-5ac17674e8e0) over an SSH forward to its loopback port 18082, with examples/windows-native/models.fragment.yml and the lane's key in NINFER_NATIVE_API_KEY. Restart: the lane's own Control-Release.ps1 -Action Restart (graceful stop, start, health wait). Stopped again afterwards, as found.",
   "rtx5090": "The production container (image cd9e10b1, profile qwen38-5090-v0.8.2) over the tailnet, with examples/manual-tunnel/models.fragment.yml. Client traffic only: no production restart was spent on this measurement."
  },
  "mock": "A scripted local Responses endpoint that tracks previous_response_id context, reports usage at a configurable bytes per token, classifies each request by the literal OMP 18.4.0 compaction prompt it carries, returns the runtime's exact error bodies (image_detail_not_supported, context_length_exceeded, request_queue_timeout) and can admit one request at a time with a deadline and slow handoff replies.",
  "source_reading": "Runtime: tool_choice none makes a request carry no tools (request.h uses_tools), so the rendered prompt lacks the tool block every other turn starts with; the admission deadline is --pending-timeout-ms, default 30000, not overridden by either lane; both lanes run one active request (RTX 5090 profiles pass --max-concurrency 1; the RTX 4090 reports device-state 2-cache+1-active). Client: compaction.asyncEnabled (default true) starts speculative compaction as context nears the threshold; OMP's OpenAI transport resends 5xx responses up to 6 attempts within its first-event watchdog."
 },
 "observations": {
  "rtx4090_async_default_config": {
   "config": "examples/manual-tunnel/fail-closed.yml as of v0.8.5 (no compaction key)",
   "outcome": "failed at turn 14 of epoch 3: 503 request_queue_timeout, inference request expired while waiting for admission",
   "background_handoffs": "three requests of 73,794, 74,608 and 75,025 prompt tokens, each reuse=root cache=0, generating 1,281, 990 and 1,644 tokens in 59.2, 56.4 and 61.4 s (the third cancelled when the turn failed)",
   "turns_behind_them": "each waiting turn's first attempt expired at 30 s (runtime requests 6, 12, 19); the resend succeeded after 79.0 and 124.8 s in epochs 1 and 2 and expired again in epoch 3 (request 20)",
   "cold_replay": "the epoch-2 resend re-prefilled 102,395 tokens from root (92.4 s to first token)",
   "compactions_committed": 2
  },
  "rtx4090_inline_config": {
   "config": "examples/manual-tunnel/fail-closed.yml with compaction.asyncEnabled false (this release)",
   "passed": true,
   "handoffs": "3 committed at 101,649, 102,730 and 102,709 tokens before; 83.7, 77.0 and 79.5 s each; summaries of 2,835-3,822 bytes",
   "turn_cost": "ordinary 23,600-token filler turns 15.3-19.7 s; the turn carrying each compaction 91.0-101.1 s (handoff plus a cold prefill of the 24,700-32,200-token compacted context); in the band just below the threshold OMP replays the whole session without previous_response_id and with max_output_tokens clamped, and the second such replay in a row re-prefilled about 102,600 tokens from root (68.1-68.4 s to first token)",
   "expired_admissions": 0,
   "restart": "graceful stop saved 1 session; the lane was ready 114.3 s after the command; the new OMP process recalled the newest control identifier",
   "durable_identifiers_recalled_after_three_compactions": "3 of 3",
   "second_run": "an earlier run of the same configuration with the identifiers planted mid-epoch also passed: handoffs of 76.3-81.4 s, 3 of 3 durable identifiers after a restart"
  },
  "rtx5090_snapcompact": {
   "config": "the same inline config; snapcompact is local, so async compaction never runs on this lane's default path",
   "passed": true,
   "compactions": "2 committed at 101,620 and 104,306 tokens before, 0.08 and 0.07 s each on the client; the next request prefilled the 56,900-57,900-token compacted context from root in 22.1-22.5 s",
   "frames": "5 frames per compaction of 196 by 71 characters in an 8x13 font, 1568 by up to 1562 pixels; the runtime's registered image ceiling is 16,777,216 pixels, so detail auto reaches the model at native resolution",
   "readback": "both durable identifiers existed at the final question only inside frames (not in the archive's head or tail text or any kept message) and both were recalled",
   "dropped": "the archives kept 84,172 and 90,314 characters and dropped 76,832 and 192,080 characters of older middle history",
   "unexplained": "in this run and both earlier client runs one chained turn with previous_response_id re-prefilled its whole context from root (101,511, 93,696 and 105,066 tokens; 43.3, 40.1 and 46.4 s to first token); cause not identified"
  },
  "mock_reproduction": {
   "single_admission_3s_deadline_45s_handoff": "v0.8.5 config: the turn behind the background handoff failed after 6 expired attempts; inline config: 0 expired attempts, the handoff ran before the turn (45.0 s) and every check passed",
   "overflow": "the runtime's HTTP 400 context_length_exceeded is classified by OMP 18.4.0 as a context overflow on both fragments: it compacts (handoff on the text model, snapcompact on the image model) and retries the turn, which succeeds"
  },
  "checkpoints_after_compaction": {
   "without_compaction": "EXP-067's proof rerun on the RTX 4090: after a restart the new process's first request reused the restored checkpoint (7,386 tokens, private_response_replay, 186 ms to first token)",
   "after_compaction": "in both inline runs the runtime logged a checkpoint restore for the session and the first request still reused nothing (32,261 and 32,215 tokens from root, 16.8 and 16.9 s to first token); after each compaction it logged refused continuation exports ('catalogued checkpoint tag mismatch', 'session is not indexed in the engine')"
  }
 },
 "decisions": {
  "shipped": "examples/manual-tunnel/fail-closed.yml, the config every route installs, sets compaction.asyncEnabled false",
  "runtime_backlog": [
   "Render tools for tool_choice none so OMP's handoff reuses the session's cache instead of re-prefilling it (56-84 s per RTX 4090 handoff).",
   "Index a transcript replay's result as the session's continuation, so OMP's consecutive replays below the threshold reuse it (68 s each on the RTX 4090).",
   "After a compaction, let the session's durable checkpoint follow the compacted lineage so a restart restores it hot.",
   "Find why one chained RTX 5090 turn per long session re-prefills from root."
  ]
 },
 "limits": [
  "One run per configuration on each lane; the async failure depends on how long the handoff takes against OMP's resend window, so its rate is not measured.",
  "Synthetic build-log filler, one fixed seed, thinking low. Durable-identifier recall is recorded, not gated, and is one observation per identifier.",
  "The RTX 5090 was not restarted after compaction (client traffic only); its post-compaction restore is not measured.",
  "The mock is a scripted endpoint; its token accounting is calibrated, not the runtime's tokenizer."
 ],
